// @check
// @error a default value must be a literal
// A default that names an EARLIER PARAMETER is rejected. A default is
// substituted into each call site and emitted in the CALLER's frame, where the
// callee's parameters do not exist — so this would either capture whatever the
// caller happens to call `a`, or need the default evaluated inside the callee,
// which is an ABI change rather than sugar.
function f(a: i32, b: i32 = a): i32 { a + b }
print(f(1))
